===Pronunciation===
* {{a|predicative only}} {{IPA|de|/oˈʁãːʃ/|/oˈʁaŋʃ/|/oˈʁɔ̃ːʃ/|/oˈʁɔŋʃ/}}
* {{a|non-predicative feminine and plural forms}} {{IPA|de|/oˈʁãːʒə/|/oˈʁaŋʒə/|/oˈʁɔ̃ːʒə/|/oˈʁɔŋʒə/}}
* {{audio|de|De-orange.ogg|Audio}}

===Adjective===
{{rfc|de|"strong nominative masculine singular (standard) oranger or (colloquial) orangener" -- this lacks the form "orange".}}
{{de-adj|stem:+[standard]:orangen[colloquial].comp.sup:orangest[standard]:orangenst[colloquial]}}

# [[#English|orange]]

====Usage notes====
* The adjective has two sets of forms. In the formal standard language, endings are added directly to the stem (''orang-''). In less formal style and in the vernacular, another set of forms is used in free variation, in which an ''-n-'' is infixed before the endings.
* It is also officially correct to leave the adjective entirely undeclined. This usage is rare, however, and seems dated.

